at least 20 people have been injured in  a car bomb that exploded in front of the  government building this is in southern  Thailand happened in the city of yalla  where officials were holding a meeting  to discuss the spread of coronavirus  Wayne hey with us now from Bangkok on  skype Wayne take us through what you  know yes well as you mentioned this took  place in yala province in the morning  this is one of the three southernmost  provinces of Thailand bordering Malaysia  and in those three southern provinces  there is an armed Muslim separatist  group operating or several groups  operating they are fighting for  independence or greater autonomy from  Thailand and have been doing so for  years Thailand is of course a  predominantly Buddhist country so these  groups regularly staged attacks in the  three southernmost provinces they are  usually relatively small in nature  usually at gun attacks small bomb  attacks targeting security forces  government buildings as was the case  just a few hours ago and also anyone  that is seemed to be sympathetic to the  government in Bangkok as I say there are  several groups operating in southern  Thailand but there really is in recent  years anyway one main group that is  believed to be behind much of the  violence that is brn Barisan revolution  a tea now or the National Revolutionary  front we believe that it's highly likely  that the brn was behind this bomb attack  outside a government building where  there were several local government  leaders meeting with military officials  as well as you say talking about  coronavirus and how best to tackle this  situation in southern Thailand what  makes this attack particularly  interesting is one of the bombs there  were two bombs outside their building  one of them was a car bomb which is it  does happen in southern Thailand but  they are relatively rare the second  thing is that we seem to have entered a  new round of peace talks beginning in  January the Thai government mess wi